## Interface: 120100
## Title: Tank Tools
## Notes: Marks enemy nameplates by threat, so yowa can see at a glance what is not yours.
## Author: mmantas
## Version: 1.1.0
## SavedVariables: TankToolsDB
## OptionalDeps: EllesmereUI
## Category: Combat

# Load order is the dependency graph, and it is the only place that graph is
# written down. Core before UI before Modules; within Core, Namespace first
# because everything hangs off it, and Events before DB because the database
# resolves on an event.
#
# Within Modules, a module that another one reads goes first: Nameplates reads
# the threat state ids at file scope.
#
# AuraRow is in UI rather than Modules because it is a widget, not a feature:
# it has no settings, no commands and no lifecycle, and the co-tank panel
# builds one the same way it builds a status bar.
#
# Features sits after DB because a flag is a saved setting like any other, and
# before State so which modules exist is settled before anything reads the
# world. Its window is in UI, after the widgets it is built from.
#
# The debuff journal is split the same way and for the same reason: the module
# records and stores, the window in UI only draws. The window loads first and
# calls into the module at runtime, never at file scope.
#
# Sounds and Symbols are data plus one function each, read by modules only at
# runtime, so their place in Core is a convention rather than a dependency:
# they sit last there, ahead of every module that plays an alert or draws a
# marker.
#
# ImportantCasts reads nothing at file scope from any other module -- it does
# not consume Threat's state map, and it derives plate/cast truth fresh every
# tick the same way Threat itself does -- so it has no ordering dependency and
# sits last.

Core\Namespace.lua
Core\Secret.lua
Core\Events.lua
Core\DB.lua
Core\Features.lua
Core\State.lua
Core\Ticker.lua
Core\Commands.lua
Core\Sounds.lua
Core\Symbols.lua

UI\Widgets.lua
UI\AuraRow.lua
UI\Options.lua
UI\Features.lua
UI\Debuffs.lua

Modules\Threat.lua
Modules\Nameplates.lua
Modules\TankWatch.lua
Modules\Debuffs.lua
Modules\ImportantCasts.lua
